# Alembic migrations

Baseline revision `001_initial_schema` executes the canonical SQL in
`database/migrations/001_initial_schema.sql`.

## Fresh database

```bash
cd backend
alembic upgrade head
```

## Existing database (already applied via SQL init)

Mark the baseline without running DDL:

```bash
cd backend
alembic stamp head
```

## New migrations

```bash
alembic revision -m "describe change"
# or autogenerate once all models exist:
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe change"
alembic upgrade head
```

Uses `DATABASE_URL` from `.env` (async URL is converted to sync `psycopg2` for Alembic).
